  "scope": "Extend the existing ModelOpt group16 BF16 software-reference Nvfp4Linear to Apple/Vulkan; re-execute CPU/CUDA with an additional nonzero subnormal-weight witness. No model artifact, quality or speed acceptance.",
  "previous_contract": "docs/evidence/correctness/nvfp4-reference-linear-2026-10-20.json",
  "integration": {
    "public_operation_unchanged": true,
    "core_or_executor_added": false,
    "apple": "Existing typed Apple native lowering and CheckTrace. Logical E4M3 scale uses byte storage only for this operation; ordinary arithmetic cannot reinterpret it as U8.",
    "vulkan": "Existing Program dispatches, original six bindings/status word. Two phases quantize A once then consume original packed W/scales; no dense W bank.",
    "math": "One private U32 IEEE F32 add/mul/div source string with small Metal/GLSL dialect wrappers. This preserves legal subnormal globals and BF16 operands without depending on native float division accuracy or F32 denormal preservation.",
    "workspace": "A QDQ uses2*M*K bytes in each backend. Apple also uses compact per-group/output status arrays and managed CheckTrace; Vulkan uses its existing status word and slot storage. These are not claims that all GPU temporary/opaque allocation equals2*M*K.",
    "cold_constant_copy": "An actual6-byte E4M3 constant exposed Vulkan non-four-byte D2D rejection. Owned padded carriers now use the existing single TransferSlot allocation for two compute-queue legs, with an intervening completion wait and explicit transfer-write/read visibility. It is cold constant materialization, not warm inference; no host payload copy. Aligned D2D remains direct and clipped spans remain rejected.",
    "output_origin": "Vulkan binding5 has no byte-origin push field, so descriptor_buffer rejects a nonzero alignment prefix and validates padded capacity. Storage is independently allocated at the same padded capacity; an odd BF16 final word writes authorized padding only."
  },
